@spec patternEditor_shelf_spec  src=tests/specs/patternEditor_shelf_spec.lua  loc=303  cases=7
@exercises keyQueue (kq), patternEditor (pe), dataStore (h.ds)
@surface   kq:fill, pe:open, pe:draw, pe:handleInput, ds:get, ds:assign
@harness   mk, reaper.GetMediaItemTake_Track

# Intent
  design/fx-patterns.md P4: the library copy shelf -- Save/Load in the pattern-editor toolbar.
  Save and Load are both chrome.drawPicker widgets, captured by kind through a fake chrome; gridPane
  is swapped for an inert stub via util._stubs so pe:draw's toolbar runs without the grid render.

# Helpers
  @fn keyId(name)  @ 11-20
  @fn setKeys(keys, mods)  @ 67-71
      -- The mini editor runs inside the modal the fill records as owner, and claims under that
      -- name, so the queue each pass reads is filled as one. See docs/keyQueue.md § Ownership.
  @fn loadPE(deps)  @ 88-99
  @fn notesBody()  @ 101-109
  @fn curveBody()  @ 111-116
  @fn withEditor(harness, body, poly)  @ 120-127
      -- Open the editor on `body`, capturing each write-through commit; get() reads the latest. hostDs is
      -- the harness ds (project scope), standing in for trackerPage's shared ds.
  @fn frame(pe, o)  @ 130-135
      -- One draw frame: queue a button press / injected input text / held keys, then draw.
  @fn input(pe, keys)  @ 137-140

# Cases
  @case 'Save stores a whitelisted copy on the host ds under a typed new name'  [harness]  @ 144-156
  @case 'Save over an existing name overwrites immediately, no confirm'  [harness]  @ 160-175
  @case 'Load rematerialises the picked body; the param tracks it'  [harness]  @ 179-195
  @case 'both pickers offer only matching kind, and matching domain for curves'  [harness]  @ 199-229
  @case 'Esc after a Load restores the modal-open snapshot, not the loaded body'  [harness]  @ 233-248
  @case 'a mono note param offers only single-lane bodies; a poly param offers multi-lane too'  [harness]  @ 252-280
  @case 'Load offers a per-row delete that drops just that name; Save offers none'  [harness]  @ 284-301

